    "body": "Ordinary sentence/Rust instructions could disturb literal operand selection or numeric admission: a 13+4 question copied 4 or returned Unknown. Continue the existing learned signed-H4 literal and admission routers so the tested prefix/suffix forms retain the correct ordered operands and use the existing lexical emitter.\n\nThe new outer artifact witness restores both prior routers and validates the complete accepted parent. Training uses 72 ordered construction examples and 745 already-open parent contexts. The evaluator independently checks ordered operand IDs and compares previous lexical outputs against the exact frozen-parent receipts.\n\nExecuted locally on retained candidate `ccbe7f2a`:\n\n- Construction 72/72; open 24/24; changed names/fact order 24/24; post-selection numeric transfers 24/24. Restoring the parent routers leaves 8/24 open answers correct.\n- All 663 main retained answers, earlier preservation panels and 72 exact prior lexical outputs pass. Earlier operators/current-query/history behavior and dependency/emitter controls remain preserved.\n- Actual native Rust API 38/38, including ordinary instructions, checkpoint import, subsequent independent answers and artifact tampering. Six read-state and six operator tests, native source guard and formatting pass.\n- Actual artifact: eight zero-allocation ingestion/generation cases, 136 checkpoint positions. Thirty actual generated Rust equalities compile and evaluate.\n\nPreserve all intermediate candidates and failures: one failed five reversed-order instruction cases; another passed the new panels but failed eleven earlier responses and was rejected. The final fit repairs these without serving exceptions. Cumulative model use is 9,047.086 / 10,350.000 seconds, including all 886.106 seconds this cycle; no cumulative allowance increase was needed. The 128 MiB storage stop margin remains.\n\nThis covers twelve authored request/placement forms and the declared numeric/name/order transfers. General prose, arbitrary instruction following, full Rust synthesis and energy advantage remain unqualified. Combined two-operation formatted responses and the new artifact's browser/WASM/HTTP path are NOT_RUN. Queue statuses are compatibility acknowledgements; the validation above was executed locally.\n\nThe artifact is local at `.uor-models/native-typed-value-2026-09-05/instruction-binding/model.json`; source, hashes, full result pointers and resources are recorded in the new result/evidence documents. Next: combine retained operator transitions with formatted output and exact intermediate dependencies.\n\nReferences #1140.\n",
